# Production build config for the web SPA.
#
# VITE_API_URL is INTENTIONALLY EMPTY so the built bundle calls the API on the
# SAME ORIGIN it was served from. That is correct for every deployment where the
# API also serves the SPA (SERVE_WEB=true) - which is all of them now.
#
# This file previously shipped `VITE_API_URL=https://192.168.1.53:3000`, a
# developer's LAN address, baked into every production build. On the AWS
# deployment (2026-07-25) that made the browser call 192.168.1.53:3000 and fail
# with "Failed to fetch" on login. It also leaked an internal IP into a repo
# that CLAUDE.md claimed was "tracked blank".
#
# Only set this if the API is genuinely on a DIFFERENT origin from the web app.
VITE_API_URL=
